//? Title: Gale–Shapley: actual deferred acceptance and safe stability checks
//? Subtitle: FIFO proposal traces, both orientations, exact stable sets and the limits of rank summaries
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given equal groups with strict complete rankings, find a one-to-one matching
with no pair that mutually prefers to abandon its assigned partners.
Deferred acceptance solves this by keeping offers tentative. A two-agent
example shows an actual displacement and the free-proposer queue.
The original five-agent program is then rerun through native fixtures,
orientation helpers and rank summaries. Exhaustive small examples separate
proposer-optimal stability from a claim that everyone is best off.
Actual proposal counts, structural matching validation and owned-history
admission keep the theorem, the implementation and resource limits distinct.
)

\toc

> One tentative offer is displaced

Both proposers rank reviewers 0 then 1. Reviewer 0 ranks proposer 1 above 0;
reviewer 1 ranks proposer 0 above 1. The FIFO starts [0,1].
Proposer 0 is initially held by reviewer 0, then displaced when proposer 1 arrives.
Proposer 0 returns to the queue and proposes to reviewer 1. Final partners are
P0–R1 and P1–R0, after three actual proposals.

The native diagram uses the captured decisions and queues from that execution.
The incumbent and newly-free columns use none when no such proposer exists.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gale_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/stable_matching.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::StablePreferences p{{0,1},{0,1}},r{{1,0},{0,1}};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::gale_shapley_trace(p,r,51);
  std::print("| proposal | proposer | reviewer | prior incumbent | decision | newly free | FIFO after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n");
  for(const auto& e:t.events)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",e.number,e.proposer,e.reviewer,e.held==dm::algorithms::kUnmatched?"none":std::to_string(e.held),e.decision,e.newly_free==dm::algorithms::kUnmatched?"none":std::to_string(e.newly_free),e.queue_after);
  std::print("\nFinal proposer map {}; reviewer map {}; proposals {}; free accepts {}; replacements {}; immediate rejections {}; retained entries {}; stable {}.\n",t.result.proposer_match,t.result.reviewer_match,t.result.proposals,t.work.accepted_free,t.work.replacements,t.work.rejections,t.captured_entries,dm::algorithms::is_stable(t.result,p,r));
  const auto& a=t.events.at(0);const auto& b=t.events.at(1);const auto& c=t.events.at(2);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(62,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.3;box.height=2.2;box.font_size=22;
  d.node("first",{0,0},std::format("Proposal {}\nP{} -> R{}\nR{} holds P{}\nqueue {}",a.number,a.proposer,a.reviewer,a.reviewer,a.reviewer_match[a.reviewer],a.queue_after),box)
   .node("replace",{6,0},std::format("Proposal {}\nP{} -> R{}\nDisplace P{}\nqueue {}",b.number,b.proposer,b.reviewer,b.newly_free,b.queue_after),box)
   .node("last",{12,0},std::format("Proposal {}\nP{} -> R{}\nR{} holds P{}\nqueue {}",c.number,c.proposer,c.reviewer,c.reviewer,c.reviewer_match[c.reviewer],c.queue_after),box)
   .edge("first","replace","next in FIFO").edge("replace","last",std::format("P{} retries",b.newly_free))
   .text({6,2.8},"Deferred acceptance: being held is not final",27)
   .text({6,-2.3},std::format("Actual final partners: P0-R{}, P1-R{}",t.result.proposer_match[0],t.result.proposer_match[1]),26)
   .save_svg("build/gale_tiny.svg");
  if(t.result.proposals!=3||t.work.replacements!=1||!dm::algorithms::is_stable(t.result,p,r))throw std::runtime_error("tiny FIFO control");
}
