> Safe candidates and conservative whole-history admission

Structural feasibility is checked before indexing a candidate's partner IDs.
A malformed candidate returns false from is_stable; invalid preferences still
throw. Diagnostic flags distinguish malformed maps from valid partial or
unstable perfect matchings. An empty witness list certifies nothing when
feasible=false. Proposal-count metadata is ignored by stability checks.

Full preference validation precedes optional quotas and can allocate O(n)
duplicate-detection scratch. A trace's admission then precedes quadratic rank
tables, matching state and input/history copies. For n agents per side its
conservative entry bound is

$$
3n+3n^2+Q(n)(1+5n).
$$
\alttext(Whole trace entries comprise three preference-or-rank matrices with their row records, plus the proposal bound times one metadata record and up to five vectors of length n.)

The three matrices are both input preference tables and the actual reviewer
inverse ranks. Each event owns next-choice indices, two partner maps and FIFO
contents before and after the decision. One record covers scalar event metadata.
Entries are not bytes or peak RAM; ordinary final maps, work/root metadata,
working state and allocator bytes are excluded. The default cap is one million;
zero disables only the optional cap, while arithmetic and container checks remain.
There is no truncation, partial trace or caller mutation.

The tiny example actually retains 45 entries, but needs the conservative whole
bound 51. Cap 45 rejects the request before matching, while cap 51 admits it.
Blocking-pair diagnostics and enumeration use separate worst-case pair and
candidate-count limits. These limits do not share the units of the trace quota.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gale_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/stable_matching.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::StablePreferences p{{0,1},{0,1}},r{{1,0},{0,1}};
  bool denied=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::gale_shapley_trace(p,r,45);}catch(const std::length_error&){denied=true;}
  auto t=dm::algorithms::gale_shapley_trace(p,r,51);p[0].clear();r.clear();t.events[0].proposer_match[0]=99;
  const bool owned=t.proposer_preferences[0]==std::vector<std::size_t>{0,1}&&t.events[1].proposer_match[0]==dm::algorithms::kUnmatched&&t.result.proposer_match[0]==1;
  const auto common=dm::algorithms::stable_matching_common_preferences(2);
  const std::array<dm::algorithms::StableMatchingResult,4> cases{{{{0,0},{0,0},0},{{dm::algorithms::kUnmatched,1},{dm::algorithms::kUnmatched,1},0},{{1,0},{1,0},0},{{0,1},{0,1},0}}};
  const std::array<std::string,4> names{"Malformed duplicate","Feasible partial","Unstable perfect","Stable perfect"};
  std::print("| candidate | feasible | complete | stable | blocking pairs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<cases.size();++i){const auto d=dm::algorithms::stable_matching_diagnostics(cases[i],common.proposer_preferences,common.reviewer_preferences);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",names[i],d.feasible,d.complete,d.stable,d.blocking_pairs.size());}
  const auto partial=dm::algorithms::stable_matching_diagnostics(cases[1],common.proposer_preferences,common.reviewer_preferences);
  const auto& witness=partial.blocking_pairs.at(0);
  std::print("\nPartial witness P{}-R{}: proposer rank {} versus incumbent {}; reviewer rank {} versus incumbent {}. Unmatched incumbent rank is n+1.\n",witness.proposer,witness.reviewer,witness.proposer_rank,witness.proposer_partner_rank,witness.reviewer_rank,witness.reviewer_partner_rank);
  bool invalid=false,overflow=false,enumeration_cap=false,witness_cap=false;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::gale_shapley_trace({{0,0},{1,0}},common.reviewer_preferences,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid=true;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::gale_shapley_trace_entries(std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max());}catch(const std::length_error&){overflow=true;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::enumerate_stable_matchings(common.proposer_preferences,common.reviewer_preferences,1);}catch(const std::length_error&){enumeration_cap=true;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::stable_matching_diagnostics(cases[3],common.proposer_preferences,common.reviewer_preferences,3);}catch(const std::length_error&){witness_cap=true;}
  const auto empty=dm::algorithms::gale_shapley({},{});const auto ranks=dm::algorithms::stable_matching_ranks(empty,{},{});
  std::print("Trace: upper {}; actual {}; cap 45 rejected {}; cap 51 admitted true; owned after caller/event edits {}; original upper {}.\n",dm::algorithms::gale_shapley_trace_entries(2),t.captured_entries,denied,owned,dm::algorithms::gale_shapley_trace_entries(5));
  std::print("Admission/domain checks: invalid preferences before quota {}; virtual overflow rejected {}; whole enumeration cap rejected {}; worst-case witness cap rejected {}.\n",invalid,overflow,enumeration_cap,witness_cap);
  std::print("Empty: proposals {}; stable {}; trace entries {}; rank summary has agents {}; perfect permutations {}.\n",empty.proposals,dm::algorithms::is_stable(empty,{},{}),dm::algorithms::gale_shapley_trace_entries(0),ranks.has_agents,dm::algorithms::stable_matching_permutations(0));
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({51.,double(t.captured_entries),45.},{"Whole upper bound","Actual retained","Rejected cap"});
  plot.title("Whole-request admission uses 51 despite actual 45").xlab("Tiny two-agent trace").ylab("Retained-history entries; not bytes").y_limits(0,60).size(1050,520).save_svg("build/gale_controls.svg");
  if(!denied||!owned||!invalid||!overflow||!enumeration_cap||!witness_cap)throw std::runtime_error("safe feasibility and admission");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| candidate | feasible | complete | stable | blocking pairs |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: |
| Malformed duplicate | false | false | false | 0 |
| Feasible partial | true | false | false | 3 |
| Unstable perfect | true | true | false | 1 |
| Stable perfect | true | true | true | 0 |

Partial witness P0-R0: proposer rank 1 versus incumbent 3; reviewer rank 1 versus incumbent 3. Unmatched incumbent rank is n+1.
Trace: upper 51; actual 45; cap 45 rejected true; cap 51 admitted true; owned after caller/event edits true; original upper 636.
Admission/domain checks: invalid preferences before quota true; virtual overflow rejected true; whole enumeration cap rejected true; worst-case witness cap rejected true.
Empty: proposals 0; stable true; trace entries 0; rank summary has agents false; perfect permutations 1.
\image(figures/gale_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(An invalid map is rejected structurally, while a valid partial candidate exposes genuine blocking pairs. The trace quota admits the whole conservative history rather than its smaller observed output.)
\alttext(Three bars show a 51-entry upper bound,45 actual retained entries and a rejected 45-entry cap. The computed table separately distinguishes malformed, partial, unstable and stable candidates.)

Stable matching depends on the submitted preference model and the chosen proposing
side. The native APIs preserve that orientation, expose actual decisions and
validate candidate structure before making a stability claim. Rank summaries,
finite exact enumeration and resource quotas make the result inspectable without
turning ordinal preferences into a universal measure of fairness.
